.TH RITZ 1 "2026-06-29" "ritz 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ritz \- Remote Interface to Zino
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ritz
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ritz
("Remote Interface to Zino") is a Tcl/Tk graphical client for the Zino
network state monitor. It connects to a Zino server over the Zino line
protocol and lets operators browse, filter and manage cases (network
alarms): acknowledging them, setting state, adding history, and clearing
flapping ports.
.PP
Symbolic OID and MIB handling is provided by the Tnm Tcl extension; the
user interface is built with the Tix widget set.
.SH CONFIGURATION
On startup
.B ritz
sources
.I ~/.smon.tcl
and
.I ~/.ritz.tcl
if they exist. These are ordinary Tcl scripts. The scalar variables
.BR Server ", " Port ", " User " and " Secret
define the server connected to automatically at launch.
.PP
Several servers may be predefined with the parallel arrays
.BR _Server() ", " _Port() ", " _User() " and " _Secret() ","
keyed by a label of your choice. Each label then appears under
.B "File \[->] Use settings"
in the menu; selecting one and choosing
.B "File \[->] Open"
connects to that server.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.ritz.tcl
Per-user configuration (server definitions, authentication).
.TP
.I ~/.smon.tcl
Optional additional configuration, sourced before
.IR ~/.ritz.tcl .
.SH SEE ALSO
The Zino documentation.
